                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "3 to 6 weeks from application including ADCLA scrutiny and premises inspection. If KSPC registration pending, add 2-4 weeks. Patron coordinates both in parallel."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Is KSPC registration mandatory for drug licence in Karnataka?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. The qualified pharmacist must be KSPC-registered before filing. Original KSPC certificate submitted with application. Without it, the Drugs Controller will not process the application."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What are premises requirements for a pharmacy in Bangalore?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Minimum 10 sq metre carpet area for retail (15 sq metre for combined). Refrigerator for temperature-sensitive drugs, AC, adequate shelving, dispensing counter. Schedule X drugs need separate locked cabinet."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Do drug licences expire in Karnataka?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "No. Since 2018 amendment to Rule 63, licences are valid indefinitely. However, retention fee must be deposited every 5 years. Failure makes the licence void requiring fresh application."
              }
            },
