<!-- SECTION 2: OVERVIEW / INTRO + TL;DR -->
<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Drug License in Bangalore - Overview</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - Drug License in Bangalore Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p><p>A drug license is the mandatory authorisation under the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940 for any business involved in the sale, distribution, or manufacture of drugs and cosmetics in India. In Bangalore, every medical shop, pharmacy, wholesale distributor, and pharma manufacturer must obtain a licence from the Drugs Controller for the State of Karnataka before commencing operations. The Karnataka Drugs Control Department operates through an online portal at drugs.karnataka.gov.in with computerised SMS alerts.</p></p>
                </div>
                <p><p>Bangalore's pharmaceutical ecosystem is one of India's largest. Biocon in Electronic City, Strides Pharma in Bommasandra, and the healthcare corridor (Narayana Health, Manipal Hospital, Fortis, Apollo) drive demand for pharmacy licences and wholesale distribution. Retail chains like MedPlus and Apollo Pharmacy operate hundreds of outlets. Learn more about <a href="#">Drug License across India</a>.</p></p>
                <p><p>A critical Karnataka-specific step: the qualified pharmacist must first register with the Karnataka State Pharmacy Council (KSPC). Without KSPC registration, the Drugs Controller will not process the application. After drug licence, consider <a href="/gst-registration">GST Registration</a> and <a href="/shop-act-registration">Shop Act Registration</a> for complete pharmacy compliance.</p></p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What is a Drug License?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>A drug license is the mandatory legal authorisation issued under the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940 and Rules, 1945, permitting a person or entity to sell, stock, distribute, or manufacture drugs and cosmetics, subject to quality standards, premises requirements, and qualified person conditions.</p><p>The licence is issued by the ADCLA for retail, wholesale, and restricted licences. Each licence is premises-specific and requires a qualified pharmacist registered with the relevant State Pharmacy Council.</p><p>For Bangalore's pharmacy sector, whether opening a chemist shop in Jayanagar, establishing wholesale distribution in Peenya, or setting up pharma manufacturing near Electronic City, the drug licence from Karnataka Drugs Control Department is the foundational requirement. Also consider <a href="/fssai-registration">FSSAI Registration</a> for nutraceuticals and <a href="/trademark-registration">Trademark Registration</a> for your pharmacy brand.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Drug License in Bangalore:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>Form 20/21:</strong> Retail drug licence for medical shops and pharmacies</li><li><strong>Form 20B/21B:</strong> Wholesale licence for distributors, stockists, C&F agents</li><li><strong>KSPC:</strong> Karnataka State Pharmacy Council - mandatory pharmacist registration before drug licence</li><li><strong>ADCLA:</strong> Assistant Drugs Controller and Licensing Authority - grants licences for Bangalore zone</li><li><strong>Schedule X:</strong> Controlled drugs requiring lock-and-key storage with restricted access</li><li><strong>Retention Fee:</strong> Payable every 5 years to keep licence valid (post-2018 amendment)</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
