                <ul><li><strong>Form 19/19C:</strong> Statutory application. Form 19 for non-Schedule X; Form 19C for Schedule X drugs.</li><li><strong>Additional Information Sheet (AIS):</strong> Supplementary premises and operations details.</li><li><strong>KSPC Registration Certificate:</strong> Original and copy. Mandatory prerequisite in Karnataka.</li><li><strong>Premises sketch:</strong> Layout showing carpet area, storage zones, refrigerator, dispensing counter, Schedule X cabinet.</li><li><strong>Rental agreement or ownership proof:</strong> For Bangalore premises with landlord NOC.</li><li><strong>Qualified person's qualification proof:</strong> D.Pharm or B.Pharm degree and experience certificates.</li><li><strong>PAN Card and Aadhaar:</strong> Of proprietor/partners/directors.</li><li><strong>Affidavit:</strong> On Rs 20 stamp paper, notarised. Declaring D&C Act compliance.</li></ul><p><strong>Bangalore-specific tip:</strong> Karnataka requires KSPC certificate in original during application. Complete KSPC registration well before drug licence filing. Patron coordinates both in parallel.</p>

