            <h2 class="section-title">Drug License - Legal and Compliance Framework</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940:</strong> Section 18 prohibits manufacture/sale without licence. Section 27: imprisonment up to 3 years and/or fine up to Rs 1 lakh for operating without licence.</p><p><strong>D&C Rules, 1945:</strong> Rules 59-65 govern licensing. Rule 63 (post-2018): licences valid indefinitely with 5-year retention fee. Forms 19, 20, 20A, 20B, 20F, 21, 21A, 21B prescribed.</p><p><strong>Karnataka Drugs Control Department:</strong> Drugs Controller for Karnataka, Bangalore. Portal: <a href="https://drugs.karnataka.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">drugs.karnataka.gov.in</a>. SMS alerts for application tracking.</p><p><strong>KSPC:</strong> Mandatory pharmacist registration before drug licence. D.Pharm/B.Pharm required.</p><p><strong>Penalties:</strong> No licence: 3 years + Rs 1 lakh. Adulterated drugs: 5 years. Spurious drugs: 10 years to life imprisonment.</p>

